### M-security

[M-security][m-sec] is a side-project I worked on with
[IV](https://github.com/Adel-Ayoub) under [MicroClub][microclub]'s developement
departement. It's a high-performance security SDK. The core concept is to move
away all the sensitive processing into a Rust library, loaded through
`flutter-rust-bridge`, and only communicate what's necessary from/to Dart.

The Rust library handles all the annoying "security stuff" (like making sure
data doesn't hit swap, or the actual encryption algorithms), and also
interfaces with hardware features for features like [Hardware Key Derivation][hkdf]
and exposing them cleanly to Dart.

There's a lot of cool stuff going on there, if you are a mobile developer doing
sensitive stuff or needing encryption/hashing/whatever algorithms, you should
really check it out!

[m-sec]: https://github.com/MicroClub-USTHB/M-security
[microclub]: https://microclub.info
[hkdf]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HKDF
